Expected elements: present

Every must-show item renders and no must-not-show item appears: Call Trace and Event Log are one tabbed region with Call Trace open, Values is a separate pane below it, and the provenance marker is the Transaction pane's first row.

Three of the five changes verify. (1) landed — the `Synthetic demo data` badge sits on the `DATA` label line and the producer's sentences occupy a full-width row beneath, flush-left at x=1157; that block is now 234px of the pane's 827px visible height, 28.3%, down from 39-41%. (4) landed — line 29 carries a grey ⊘, line 32 a cyan ⊙. (5) landed — the exit reads `← demo`. (2) and (3) cannot be verified: no `COST · TRANSACTIONFEE` row and no decoded-input note appears above y=895, because the Transaction pane's content is cut mid-line at its bottom border.

The standing observation half-holds. Call Trace interior is y69-560 (492px); last ink is the footer at y=320, so 240px is empty — 48.8%, or 52.6% measured from the last frame divider at y=301. Inside the 47-57% band, nowhere near the 76-91% found on other subjects. But Values does not overflow here: its last row ends at y=860, leaving 34px and a dangling divider. The nav column holds 274px of dead height (33.1%) while the only overflowing pane, Transaction, sits in the other column and cannot receive it. Re-weighting the split moves slack, it does not fix the overflow.

Rating: 7/10

